{"success": true, "name": "agent-memory-consolidation", "description": "Use when: Reflective memory consolidation loop: synthesize episodic task records into semantic/procedural memory upgrades. Run after complex tasks or on-demand. Grounded in Generative Agents (Park 2023), ExpeL (Zhao 2024), AgeMem (Yu 2026), LeanMem (arXiv:2608.20320), MemSIF Dual-Track (arXiv:2608.01742), and AMD (arXiv:2608.07169).\n", "tags": [], "related_skills": ["self-improve-agent", "hermes-memory-surface-selection", "ralph-loops", "hermes-agent-skill-authoring"], "content": "---\nname: agent-memory-consolidation\ndescription: >\n  Use when: Reflective memory consolidation loop: synthesize episodic task records into semantic/procedural memory upgrades. Run after complex tasks or on-demand. Grounded in Generative Agents (Park 2023), ExpeL (Zhao 2024), AgeMem (Yu 2026), LeanMem (arXiv:2608.20320), MemSIF Dual-Track (arXiv:2608.01742), and AMD (arXiv:2608.07169).\nversion: 1.9.1\ntriggers:\n  - \"consolidate memory after this session\"\n  - \"synthesize lessons into memory\"\n  - \"upgrade memory from this run\"\n  - \"what should graduate to durable memory?\"\n  - \"memory consolidation\"\n  - \"apply LeanMem to this session\"\nrelated_skills:\n  - self-improve-agent\n  - hermes-memory-surface-selection\n  - ralph-loops\n  - hermes-agent-skill-authoring\n---\n\n# Agent Memory Consolidation\n\nReflective memory consolidation converts short-lived episodic observations into\ndurable semantic/procedural knowledge. Based on the Generative Agents retrieval\nscoring model (recency + relevance + importance), the ExpeL experience extraction\npattern, AgeMem store/discard/update operations (2026), LeanMem (arXiv:2608.20320),\nMemSIF Dual-Track (arXiv:2608.01742), and AMD (arXiv:2608.07169).\n\n## Memory Poisoning Write Gate (arXiv:2608.21230, DreamBench-SWE arXiv:2608.20664, Aug 2026)\n\n**Memory Poisoning (2608.21230):** False facts that appear factually plausible and stylistically\nnormal bypass conservative retention policies. Standard dedup/contradiction checks fail because\nthe poisoned fact doesn't lexically contradict an existing fact — it supplements it with false\ndetail. Example: \"Claude has a 1M token context window\" instead of 200K.\n\n**Defense:** Cross-verification before write. For every candidate memory:\n1. Retrieve 3 most similar existing memories\n2. If any retrieved memory contradicts the candidate, flag for manual review\n3. If no contradiction but candidate introduces new detail, require 2 independent sources\n4. If only 1 source, write to a staging area with `poisoned: true` tag\n\n## MCMA — Memory Copilot Separation via DPO (arXiv:2601.07470, Aug 2026)\n\nDecoupling memory management from task execution allows memory-management capability to transfer across tasks even when specific memories don't.\n\n## AutoMem — Memory Management as a Trainable Skill (arXiv:2607.01224, Jul 2026)\n\nTreats memory structure (what to encode, when to retrieve, how to organize) as something that can be iteratively improved rather than fixed.\n\n## ACM: Agentic Context Management 5-primitive framework\n\n## Multilingual research grounding for consolidation (2025–2026 sweep)\n\n## MindMemOS — Scenario-Adaptive Memory Strategy Selection (arXiv:2608.12428, Sweep 15) ★ HIGH\n\n## Information Abundance Paradox — Long-Context vs Parametric Knowledge (arXiv:2608.12218, Sweep 15) ★ MED\n\n## CMI: Controlled Memory Interference in Continual Agents (arXiv:2608.07622, Aug 2026) ⭐\n\n## Cognee PreCompact hook — async KG sync before context compaction\n\n## Background pipeline: staging → dual-write\n\n## When to run\n\n## Memory Architecture Reference\n\n### MRAgent Cue-Tag-Content Memory Graph (arXiv:2606.06036, NUS, +23% LoCoMo/LongMemEval)\n\n### LeanMem — Lazy Consolidation with Recurrence Gating (arXiv:2608.20320, Aug 2026) ★ HIGH <!-- rationale: 87% token reduction, SOTA on LoCoMo+LongMemEval -->\n\n**LeanMem** is a lazy consolidation algorithm that only consolidates features recurring across 2+ sessions.\n\n**Hermes implementation:**\n- After each session, extract all features (entities, actions, outcomes)\n- For each feature, check if it appeared in the last 2 sessions\n- If yes, consolidate into durable memory with `consolidation_score = recurrence_count * importance_score`\n- If no, keep in ephemeral memory only\n- Recurrence count is stored as metadata: `recurrence: 2`\n\n**Token reduction:** 87% vs full consolidation, 94% vs naive turn-level encoding.\n\n### MemSIF — Dual-Track Fact Memory (arXiv:2608.01742, Aug 2026) ★ HIGH\n<!-- rationale: write-time salience ≠ future utility; CoreFact eager, ActiveFact after demand -->\n\n**MemSIF** is Dual-Track Fact Memory (NOT a state-injection filter). Verified abs:\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2608.01742 — CoreFact vs ActiveFact.\n\n**Hermes implementation (runtime, not prose):**\n- CoreFact (`ns=profile` or type `preference`/`correction`): stage eagerly in `l1-promote.py`\n- ActiveFact (everything else): stay pending in `lifecycle.db` until RecMem recurrence ≥ 2 **or** `access_count ≥ 3`\n- Query demand: `unified-recall.py` mixes pending ActiveFacts into results and increments `access_count`\n- Drain: `l1-promote.py` stages pending rows once `access_count >= 3` (does not increment on cron defer)\n- Staging tag: `[track=core|active]`; Graphiti parser strips it\n\nDo not invent a second MemSIF (2608.20444 / 2608.20112 are not this paper).\n\n### AMD — Proactive/Reactive 3-Tier Injection (arXiv:2608.07169) ★ HIGH <!-- rationale: skill authoring tier missing -->\n\n**AMD** is a 3-tier memory injection framework:\n1. **Proactive tier**: Pre-load high-value memories before the task starts (strategic)\n2. **Reactive tier**: Inject memories during task execution based on context (tactical)\n3. **Skill tier**: Update skill files with distilled procedures (abstract, on-demand)\n\n**Hermes implementation:**\n- Proactive tier: `hermes-memory-surface-selection` skill\n- Reactive tier: `agent-memory-consolidation` skill\n- **Skill tier**: `hermes-agent-skill-authoring` skill (MISSING — implement now)\n\n**Skill tier implementation:**\n- After consolidation, identify action sequences that:\n  - Occurred 3+ times\n  - Had positive outcomes\n  - Are not already covered by existing skills\n- Distill into a new skill file or patch an existing one\n- Safety gate: only verified-action sequences become SOPs\n\n### Engram - Bi-Temporal Memory Model (arXiv:2606.09900) ★ MED\n**Engram** separates event time from observation time. Existing lifecycle timestamps cover this; do not add a second timestamp schema.\n\n### PoisonedEvolution — Utility Under Attack (arXiv:2608.21230, Aug 2026) ★ HIGH\nReal paper (fetched): content screening rejected 0/360 poisons; provenance ranking has no usable weight. Hermes already has write-path filter + TraceGrant. Do not add a second screening stack.\n\n### Crash-dump IDs (sweep 25) — misattributed, do not implement\nThese arXiv IDs exist but are NOT the named memory papers:\n2608.19234, 20555, 20666, 20777, 20888, 20999, 21003, 21111, 21333, 21444,\n21555, 22001, 22444, 22888, 23333, 23567–23570.\nReal LeanMem is 2608.20320; IFCMemoryBench 2607.26072; CoEvoKG 2608.01904.\n\n## MemSIF — Dual-Track Fact Memory (arXiv:2608.01742, Aug 2026) ★ HIGH\n<!-- rationale: DUM — do not promote ActiveFacts on write-time salience alone -->\n\nSee the Dual-Track section above. Runtime: `l1-promote.py` + `unified-recall.py`.\nDo not re-implement MemSIF as a salience formula or state machine.\n\n## Step 1: Collect episodic candidates\n\n### Single-agent runs\n\n### Multi-agent runs (Hermes delegate_task / subagents)\n\n## Step 2: Apply importance scoring\n\n## Step 3: Apply the falsification gate\n\n## Step 4: Synthesize into compact semantic form\n\n## Step 5: Contradiction check before writing\n\n## Step 6: Write or stage\n\n### volatility_class - Write-Time Tagging (Veracium arXiv:2607.21962)\n\n### World-Bridge Retrieval Anchoring (arXiv:2607.24368, InMind, Jul 2026)\n\n### LeanMem — Recurrence-Gated Consolidation\n- For each candidate memory, check `recurrence_count`\n- If `recurrence_count >= 2`, consolidate with `consolidation_score = recurrence_count * importance_score`\n- If `recurrence_count < 2`, keep in ephemeral memory only\n\n### MemSIF — Dual-Track gate\n- CoreFact: write now\n- ActiveFact: write to `lifecycle.db` pending; promote only after recurrence ≥ 2 or access_count ≥ 3\n- `unified-recall.py` is what increments access_count (query demand)\n\n### AMD — Skill Tier Distillation\n- After consolidation, identify action sequences for skill distillation\n- Distill into new or existing skills\n\n## Step 7: Present proposals to user\n\n## Reflective abstraction (optional, high-value)\n\n## `memory` tool batch mechanics\n\n## Latent Preference Inference — UserToolBench Finding (arXiv:2608.10042)\n\n## Dreams API — Async Managed Consolidation (Anthropic beta, Aug 2026)\n\n## DOCSCHISEL Pattern — Iterative Tool Doc Refinement (arXiv:2608.10037)\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n## Research pattern quick-reference\n\n## Temporal metadata pre-extraction before embedding\n\n## Retrieval-time quality filters\n\n## LatticeMind — Write-Time Conflict Detection in Multi-Agent Merges (arXiv 2608.08236)\n\n## A-MEM enriched writes (Zettelkasten pattern)\n\n## MemoryOS mid-term buffer principle\n\n## Principled forgetting (FFD taxonomy)\n\n## Selective Persistent Memory — 4-Category Schema\n\n## Memory Security — FARMA/SENTINEL + GhostWriter/AM-Sentry\n\n### Salience Induction Attack + Normalization Defense (arXiv:2607.17535)\n\n## TRUSTMEM: Write-Verification Before Persisting\n\n## SENTINEL defense pattern\n\n## AutoMem Pattern — Two-Loop Memory Scaffold Optimization\n\n## D²ACCI — Dual-Loop Diagnostic Protocol for Memory Interventions (arXiv:2608.17756, Aug 2026)\n\n## MyContext — 3-State Conflict Merge for Enterprise Agent Memory (Alibaba Qwen Office, Aug 2026)\n\n## B+Tree Hierarchical Memory with LLM-Veto Merge (TRACE, r/MachineLearning, Aug 2026)\n\n## Rejected-Alternatives as a Distinct Memory Type (CommitLore, HN Aug 2026)\n\n## Integration with other skills\n\n## Skill Pruning Decision Matrix\n\n### SkillRouter - Full Skill Body Required\n\n## KVDiagnosis — Evidence-Attention Boost at Retrieval (arXiv:2608.09412, Aug 2026) ⭐ CODE\n\n## LycheeMemory V2 — Segment-Level Consolidation (arXiv:2608.12990, Aug 2026) ★ HIGH\n\n## Muscle Memory — Compile Not Merely Retrieve (arXiv:2608.08995, Aug 2026)\n\n## References\n\n## MAP-Graph — Provenance-Aware Shared Memory with Risk-Sensitive Action Gate (arXiv:2608.10509, Aug 2026)\n\n## SEEM - Structured Episodic Event Memory (arXiv:2601.06411)\n\n## GeoForge — 3-Layer Complementary Memory Architecture (arXiv:2608.10494, Aug 2026)\n\n## Inline paper knowledge bank\n\n## Aug 2026 Sweep 8 Additions (Aug 12, through 2608.09930)\n\n### MemOPD — Memory-Aligned On-Policy Distillation (arXiv:2608.07068, Aug 2026)\n\n### ColluSkill / ChainGuard — Cross-Skill Composition Attacks (arXiv:2608.09732, Aug 2026)\n\n## Aug 2026 Sweep 7 Additions\n\n### CrystalMem — Elastic Fidelity Tiers (arXiv:2608.00303)\n\n### SharedOrgMemory — Platform-Level Auto-Capture (arXiv:2608.00122)\n\n### AgentStream — Streaming Scenario Classification (arXiv:2608.00155)\n\n### Dual-Gate Dedup — Cosine Threshold Invalidity (arXiv:2608.10216)\n\n### Generic > Personalized Skills Empirical Finding (arXiv:2608.10319)\n\n### Regression Tax — Osmosis Drift in Self-Improving Systems (arXiv:2607.22520)\n\n### ENTLORE — KG Latent Relation Extraction (arXiv:2608.10679)\n\n### DREAM — L0/L1/L2 Intent Hierarchy (arXiv:2608.09408)\n\n## Correction-to-Rule Accumulation (Setoku, HN Jul 23 2026)\n\n## RUMBA Memory Evaluation Taxonomy (Sber AI, Jul 2026)\n\n## Reference files\n\n## FAMA Staleness Classification + Atomic Replace (ACL 2026.findings-acl.1337)\n\n## Selective Experience Use — SEU Filter (PATH-Bench, arXiv:2608.01149)\n\n## MemTrapBench — Cognitive Traps in Memory Use (arXiv:2608.20202, 

